{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:02:12.175864647Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"echo \"=== secret keys in the real keyring ===\"; gpg --list-secret-keys --with-colons 2\u003e/dev/null | awk -F: '/^sec:/{k=$5} /^fpr:/{f=$10} /^uid:/{print f\" \"$10; f=\"\"}' | head -6; echo \"=== pass entries under beadle ===\"; pass ls beadle 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -6; echo \"=== ethos identity gpg fields ===\"; ethos identity get claude 2\u003e/dev/null | grep -iE \"gpg|key\" | head -4; ethos identity get jmf 2\u003e/dev/null | grep -iE \"gpg|key\" | head -4","description":"Check keyring, pass entries, and ethos gpg fields"},"tool_input_hash":"4a18167ba637f02fd14cdb5280d37325f0d13c6975a021b9ee757e841eaae216","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== secret keys in the real keyring ===\\\"; gpg --list-secret-keys --with-colons 2\\u003e/dev/null | awk -F: '/^sec:/{k=$5} /^fpr:/{f=$10} /^uid:/{print f\\\" \\\"$10; f=\\\"\\\"}' | head -6;..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:02:28.773702405Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"echo \"=== are the keys passphrase-protected? (P = protected) ===\"; gpg-connect-agent 'keyinfo --list' /bye 2\u003e/dev/null | awk '{print $3, $7}' | head -6; echo \"=== do they carry expiry? (daemon requires it) ===\"; for f in 24A9B79FA94101C11F09A011CEE670F91FB96851 2C7C808DEC5ECC59A23E4358C48E101AB522FB17; do printf \"%s \" \"${f:0:16}\"; gpg --list-keys --with-colons \"$f\" 2\u003e/dev/null | awk -F: '/^pub:/{print ($7==\"\"?\"NO EXPIRY\":\"expires \"$7)}'; done","description":"Check key protection and expiry"},"tool_input_hash":"c4c45f8e47b231dea8b9929581099a1abb207c9c87f29dd7595b9ec6d7e4e643","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== are the keys passphrase-protected? (P = protected) ===\\\"; gpg-connect-agent 'keyinfo --list' /bye 2\\u003e/dev/null | awk '{print $3, $7}' | head -6; echo \\\"=== do they carry exp..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:02:41.718263475Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"for f in 24A9B79FA94101C11F09A011CEE670F91FB96851 2C7C808DEC5ECC59A23E4358C48E101AB522FB17; do echo \"=== ${f:0:16} ===\"; gpg --list-keys --with-colons \"$f\" 2\u003e/dev/null | awk -F: '$1==\"pub\"||$1==\"sub\"{printf \"  %-4s cap=%-4s expires=%s\\n\", $1, $12, ($7==\"\"?\"NEVER\":strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\",$7))}'; done","description":"Precisely check expiry on primary and subkeys"},"tool_input_hash":"a056b052a1d1549c6a1d0fbcce1b11c9d06f1b2581433da37a32d217c549c7d0","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"for f in 24A9B79FA94101C11F09A011CEE670F91FB96851 2C7C808DEC5ECC59A23E4358C48E101AB522FB17; do echo \\\"=== ${f:0:16} ===\\\"; gpg --list-keys --with-colons \\\"$f\\\" 2\\u003e/dev/null | awk -F: '..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:07:33.015146034Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"AskUserQuestion","tool_input":{"annotations":{"The daemon's authorizer key must have an expiry (ARCHITECTURE.md invariant, enforced at signing). Your key never expires, so it cannot sign recipes. Claude's key expires 2027-08-29 and works — but using it means the agent authorizes its own recipes. Which key should the scripts configure?":{"preview":"gpg --quick-set-expire 24A9B79F... 2y\ngpg --quick-set-expire 24A9B79F... 2y '*'\n  (primary AND signing subkey --\n   expiry.go checks both)\n\nTHEN\n  authorizer = [REDACTED:email]\n  agent cannot sign its own recipes\n\nNOTE\n  this key also unlocks your pass\n  store -- setting an expiry does not\n  break decryption of existing entries,\n  but it will need renewing in 2y or\n  signing starts failing"}},"answers":{"The daemon's authorizer key must have an expiry (ARCHITECTURE.md invariant, enforced at signing). Your key never expires, so it cannot sign recipes. Claude's key expires 2027-08-29 and works — but using it means the agent authorizes its own recipes. Which key should the scripts configure?":"Set an expiry on your key (Recommended)"},"questions":[{"header":"Authorizer key","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"description":"gpg --quick-set-expire on 24A9B79F, then use it as authorizer. Preserves the design: a human authorizes what the agent may run. One command, no new key to manage.","label":"Set an expiry on your key (Recommended)","preview":"gpg --quick-set-expire 24A9B79F... 2y\ngpg --quick-set-expire 24A9B79F... 2y '*'\n  (primary AND signing subkey --\n   expiry.go checks both)\n\nTHEN\n  authorizer = [REDACTED:email]\n  agent cannot sign its own recipes\n\nNOTE\n  this key also unlocks your pass\n  store -- setting an expiry does not\n  break decryption of existing entries,\n  but it will need renewing in 2y or\n  signing starts failing"},{"description":"Works immediately, no key changes. But the agent's own key authorizes the agent's recipes, so the signature proves the file is unmodified rather than that a human approved it.","label":"Use Claude's key as authorizer","preview":"authorizer = 2C7C808D (claude)\n\nWHAT THE SIGNATURE STILL PROVES\n  the recipe file was not tampered\n  with after signing\n\nWHAT IT NO LONGER PROVES\n  that a human authorized it -- the\n  agent holds the key and could sign\n  any recipe it wrote\n\nZero-agent-authority becomes an\nintegrity guarantee, not an\nauthorization one. Defensible for a\ndemo; worth a bead if it persists."},{"description":"A new key used only for signing recipes, held by you, with an expiry. Cleanest separation — not your identity key, not the agent's — but one more key to store and back up.","label":"Mint a dedicated authorizer key","preview":"gpg --quick-generate-key \\\n  \"Beadle Authorizer \[REDACTED:email]\u003e\" \\\n  ed25519 sign 2y\n\nPROS\n  purpose-built, expiry from birth,\n  revoking it does not affect your\n  identity key or pass store\n\nCONS\n  a third key to back up and remember\n  the passphrase for; if it is lost,\n  every signed recipe must be re-signed"}],"question":"The daemon's authorizer key must have an expiry (ARCHITECTURE.md invariant, enforced at signing). Your key never expires, so it cannot sign recipes. Claude's key expires 2027-08-29 and works — but using it means the agent authorizes its own recipes. Which key should the scripts configure?"}]},"tool_input_hash":"e2fa6da0fa7d1f3ffe8b2e3d64c7b3bfc46469126ec0ce97438928869360be25","tool_input_preview":"{\"annotations\":{\"The daemon's authorizer key must have an expiry (ARCHITECTURE.md invariant, enforced at signing). Your key never expires, so it cannot sign recipes. Claude's key expires 2027-08-29 an..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:08:26.036131578Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Configure beadle-daemon's authorizer key: write ~/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json.\n# Usage: beadle-recipes-init.sh --apply [--fingerprint FPR] [--repo DIR] [--force]\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Safety class: DESTRUCTIVE (writes ~/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json). Previews\n# by default; --apply is required, per punt-kit/standards/shell.md.\n#\n# daemon.json names the ONE key whose signature beadle-daemon will accept on a\n# recipe file. That key is an authorizer, not an owner: it decides what the\n# agent is permitted to run. Point it at the agent's own key and the agent can\n# sign whatever it writes, which reduces the signature to an integrity check\n# and removes the authorization it is there to provide. So this script defaults\n# to a human key and says so.\n#\n# It reads the fingerprint from `pass` (a single source both humans and scripts\n# can share) and never accepts a secret on the command line. A fingerprint is\n# not itself secret, but keeping it beside the signing passphrase means one\n# place to look and one place to rotate.\n#\n# It will NOT modify your GPG key. beadle rejects non-expiring signing keys\n# (internal/pgp/expiry.go, an ARCHITECTURE.md invariant), and a great many\n# personal keys never expire -- so this checks and prints the exact command,\n# rather than silently reaching into the operator's identity key.\n\nreadonly PASS_FPR_ENTRY='beadle/authorizer-fingerprint'\nreadonly PASS_PHRASE_ENTRY='beadle/gpg-passphrase'\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" \u0026\u0026 pwd)\"\nREPO_DIR=\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../beadle\"\nAPPLY=false\nFORCE=false\nFINGERPRINT=''\n\nusage() {\n  cat \u003c\u003cEOF\nUsage: $(basename \"$0\") --apply [--fingerprint FPR] [--repo DIR] [--force]\n\nPreviews by default. Pass --apply to write daemon.json.\n\n  --apply           Perform the write. Required.\n  --fingerprint FPR 40-hex authorizer key. Default: read from\n                    \\`pass ${PASS_FPR_ENTRY}\\`.\n  --repo DIR        beadle checkout (default: the ../beadle sibling of this\n                    script's directory).\n  --force           Overwrite an existing daemon.json.\nEOF\n}\n\ndie() { printf 'error: %s\\n' \"$1\" \u003e\u00262; exit 2; }\nok()  { printf '  \\033[32m✓\\033[0m %s\\n' \"$1\"; }\nbad() { printf '  \\033[31m✗\\033[0m %s\\n' \"$1\"; }\nsec() { printf '\\n\\033[1m%s\\033[0m\\n' \"$1\"; }\n\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --apply)       APPLY=true; shift ;;\n    --force)       FORCE=true; shift ;;\n    --fingerprint) FINGERPRINT=\"${2:?--fingerprint needs a value}\"; shift 2 ;;\n    --repo)        REPO_DIR=\"${2:?--repo needs a directory}\"; shift 2 ;;\n    -h|--help)     usage; exit 0 ;;\n    *)             die \"unknown argument: $1\" ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\nDAEMON=\"${REPO_DIR}/beadle-daemon\"\nCONF=\"${HOME}/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json\"\n\nsec 'Resolving authorizer key'\n\nif [[ -z \"${FINGERPRINT}\" ]]; then\n  if ! FINGERPRINT=$(pass show \"${PASS_FPR_ENTRY}\" 2\u003e/dev/null | head -1); then\n    die \"no --fingerprint given and \\`pass ${PASS_FPR_ENTRY}\\` is unreadable.\n       Store it once:  pass insert -e ${PASS_FPR_ENTRY}\n       Or pass --fingerprint \u003c40-hex\u003e explicitly.\"\n  fi\n  ok \"fingerprint from pass (${PASS_FPR_ENTRY})\"\nelse\n  ok 'fingerprint from --fingerprint'\nfi\n\nFINGERPRINT=\"${FINGERPRINT//[[:space:]]/}\"\n[[ \"${FINGERPRINT}\" =~ ^[0-9A-Fa-f]{40}$ ]] \\\n  || die \"not a 40-hex OpenPGP fingerprint: ${FINGERPRINT}\"\n\nuid=$(gpg --list-keys --with-colons \"${FINGERPRINT}\" 2\u003e/dev/null \\\n      | awk -F: '/^uid:/{print $10; exit}')\n[[ -n \"${uid}\" ]] || die \"key ${FINGERPRINT} is not in this keyring.\n       beadle verifies against it at load time; import it first.\"\nok \"in keyring: ${uid}\"\n\n# beadle checks the primary key AND any signing-capable subkey, so check both.\n# A key with a non-expiring signing subkey is rejected even if the primary has\n# an expiry, which is easy to miss when only the primary is renewed.\nsec 'Checking the expiry invariant'\nnever=$(gpg --list-keys --with-colons \"${FINGERPRINT}\" 2\u003e/dev/null |\n        awk -F: '($1==\"pub\" || $1==\"sub\") \u0026\u0026 $12 ~ /s/ \u0026\u0026 $7==\"\" {print $1}')\nif [[ -n \"${never}\" ]]; then\n  bad \"key has a non-expiring signing component: ${never//$'\\n'/, }\"\n  cat \u003c\u003cEOF\n\n  beadle refuses non-expiring signing keys (internal/pgp/expiry.go; an\n  ARCHITECTURE.md invariant), so signing would fail after this script wrote a\n  daemon.json naming it. Set an expiry on the primary AND its subkeys:\n\n      gpg --quick-set-expire ${FINGERPRINT} 2y\n      gpg --quick-set-expire ${FINGERPRINT} 2y '*'\n\n  Then re-run. Renewing is not destructive -- it does not invalidate existing\n  signatures, and it does not affect decryption of an existing pass store.\nEOF\n  exit 1\nfi\nok 'primary and signing subkeys all carry an expiry'\n\nsec 'Signing credential'\nif pass show \"${PASS_PHRASE_ENTRY}\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261; then\n  ok \"passphrase available (pass ${PASS_PHRASE_ENTRY})\"\nelse\n  # Not fatal: an unprotected key needs none, and beadle's own error names the\n  # chain if one turns out to be required.\n  printf '  \\033[33m·\\033[0m no %s in pass -- fine for an unprotected key;\\n' \"${PASS_PHRASE_ENTRY}\"\n  printf '      if signing later fails for want of one: pass insert %s\\n' \"${PASS_PHRASE_ENTRY}\"\nfi\n\nsec 'Target'\nif [[ -f \"${CONF}\" ]] \u0026\u0026 ! \"${FORCE}\"; then\n  bad \"${CONF} already exists (pass --force to overwrite)\"\n  printf '      current: %s\\n' \"$(grep -o '\"owner_gpg_key_id\"[^,}]*' \"${CONF}\" 2\u003e/dev/null || echo '(unreadable)')\"\n  exit 1\nfi\nprintf '  %s\\n' \"${CONF}\"\n\nif ! \"${APPLY}\"; then\n  sec 'Preview (no --apply)'\n  printf '  would write daemon.json naming %s\\n' \"${FINGERPRINT}\"\n  printf '  would run: %s init --fingerprint \u003cfpr\u003e%s\\n' \"${DAEMON}\" \"$(\"${FORCE}\" \u0026\u0026 echo ' --force' || true)\"\n  printf '\\n  no changes made. Re-run with --apply to write.\\n\\n'\n  exit 0\nfi\n\n[[ -x \"${DAEMON}\" ]] || die \"beadle-daemon not built. Run: make -C ${REPO_DIR} build-daemon\"\n\nsec 'Writing'\nargs=(init --fingerprint \"${FINGERPRINT}\")\n\"${FORCE}\" \u0026\u0026 args+=(--force)\n\"${DAEMON}\" \"${args[@]}\"\nok 'daemon.json written'\nprintf '\\n  Next: %s/beadle-recipes-install.sh --apply\\n\\n' \"${SCRIPT_DIR}\"\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes/.bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh"},"tool_input_hash":"a9b9ee5d2e6859ed121e72c753448cd152f6c25f249cb46d99cd258ddcd833cb","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Configure beadle-daemon's authorizer key: write ~/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json.\\n# Usage: beadle-recipes-init.sh --apply [--fingerprint FPR] [--repo DIR] [--force]\\..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:08:57.48920507Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Sign beadle's example recipes and install them where the daemon loads them.\n# Usage: beadle-recipes-install.sh --apply [--recipe NAME] [--repo DIR] [--force]\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Safety class: DESTRUCTIVE (writes ~/.punt-labs/beadle/commands/ and signs with\n# the operator's real key). Previews by default; --apply is required, per\n# punt-kit/standards/shell.md.\n#\n# The authorizer key is read from daemon.json, never from a flag -- the daemon\n# verifies against exactly that key at load time, so resolving it from anywhere\n# else would let this script install recipes the daemon then refuses. Run\n# beadle-recipes-init.sh first if daemon.json does not exist.\n#\n# Signing is done in the commands directory, on a copy, and a recipe that fails\n# to sign or verify is REMOVED rather than left behind: LoadCommands rejects an\n# unsigned file (correctly) but logs an error for it on every startup, so a\n# half-installed recipe becomes permanent noise pointing at the wrong problem.\n#\n# No secret is passed on the command line. beadle resolves the signing\n# passphrase itself through the credential chain (pass -\u003e file -\u003e env), and its\n# error names that chain if one is needed and missing.\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" \u0026\u0026 pwd)\"\nREPO_DIR=\"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../beadle\"\nCOMMANDS_DIR=\"${HOME}/.punt-labs/beadle/commands\"\nAPPLY=false\nFORCE=false\nONLY=''\n\nusage() {\n  cat \u003c\u003cEOF\nUsage: $(basename \"$0\") --apply [--recipe NAME] [--repo DIR] [--force]\n\nPreviews by default. Pass --apply to sign and install.\n\n  --apply       Perform the install. Required.\n  --recipe NAME Install one recipe by name (default: every\n                examples/recipes/*.yaml).\n  --repo DIR    beadle checkout (default: the ../beadle sibling of this\n                script's directory).\n  --force       Replace a recipe already installed in the commands directory.\nEOF\n}\n\ndie() { printf 'error: %s\\n' \"$1\" \u003e\u00262; exit 2; }\nok()  { printf '  \\033[32m✓\\033[0m %s\\n' \"$1\"; }\nbad() { printf '  \\033[31m✗\\033[0m %s\\n' \"$1\"; }\nskip(){ printf '  \\033[33m·\\033[0m %s\\n' \"$1\"; }\nsec() { printf '\\n\\033[1m%s\\033[0m\\n' \"$1\"; }\n\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --apply)   APPLY=true; shift ;;\n    --force)   FORCE=true; shift ;;\n    --recipe)  ONLY=\"${2:?--recipe needs a name}\"; shift 2 ;;\n    --repo)    REPO_DIR=\"${2:?--repo needs a directory}\"; shift 2 ;;\n    -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;\n    *)         die \"unknown argument: $1\" ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\nDAEMON=\"${REPO_DIR}/beadle-daemon\"\nSRC_DIR=\"${REPO_DIR}/examples/recipes\"\nCONF=\"${HOME}/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json\"\n\nsec 'Preflight'\n\n[[ -d \"${SRC_DIR}\" ]] || die \"no recipes at ${SRC_DIR} (wrong --repo?)\"\nok \"source: ${SRC_DIR}\"\n\nif [[ ! -f \"${CONF}\" ]]; then\n  die \"no ${CONF}.\n       beadle-daemon loads zero commands without it, so a signed recipe would\n       sit unread. Run: ${SCRIPT_DIR}/beadle-recipes-init.sh --apply\"\nfi\nFPR=$(grep -oE '[0-9A-Fa-f]{40}' \"${CONF}\" 2\u003e/dev/null | head -1 || true)\n[[ -n \"${FPR}\" ]] || die \"no 40-hex fingerprint found in ${CONF}\"\nok \"authorizer from daemon.json: ${FPR:0:16}...\"\n\nrecipes=()\nwhile IFS= read -r f; do recipes+=(\"$f\"); done \u003c \u003c(find \"${SRC_DIR}\" -maxdepth 1 -name '*.yaml' | sort)\n[[ ${#recipes[@]} -gt 0 ]] || die \"no *.yaml in ${SRC_DIR}\"\n\nif [[ -n \"${ONLY}\" ]]; then\n  match=\"\"\n  for f in \"${recipes[@]}\"; do\n    [[ \"$(basename \"$f\" .yaml)\" == \"${ONLY}\" ]] \u0026\u0026 match=\"$f\"\n  done\n  [[ -n \"${match}\" ]] || die \"no recipe named ${ONLY} in ${SRC_DIR}\"\n  recipes=(\"${match}\")\nfi\nok \"${#recipes[@]} recipe(s) selected\"\n\nsec 'Plan'\ninstalled=0\nfor f in \"${recipes[@]}\"; do\n  name=$(basename \"$f\" .yaml)\n  dest=\"${COMMANDS_DIR}/${name}.yaml\"\n  if [[ -f \"${dest}\" ]] \u0026\u0026 ! \"${FORCE}\"; then\n    skip \"${name} -- already installed, would skip (--force to replace)\"\n  else\n    printf '  %s -\u003e %s\\n' \"${name}\" \"${dest}\"\n    installed=$((installed + 1))\n  fi\ndone\n\nif ! \"${APPLY}\"; then\n  sec 'Preview (no --apply)'\n  printf '  would sign %d recipe(s) with %s and install into\\n' \"${installed}\" \"${FPR:0:16}...\"\n  printf '  %s\\n' \"${COMMANDS_DIR}\"\n  printf '\\n  no changes made. Re-run with --apply to install.\\n\\n'\n  exit 0\nfi\n\n[[ -x \"${DAEMON}\" ]] || die \"beadle-daemon not built. Run: make -C ${REPO_DIR} build-daemon\"\n\nsec 'Installing'\nmkdir -p \"${COMMANDS_DIR}\"\nchmod 700 \"${COMMANDS_DIR}\"\nfailed=0\ndone_n=0\n\nfor f in \"${recipes[@]}\"; do\n  name=$(basename \"$f\" .yaml)\n  dest=\"${COMMANDS_DIR}/${name}.yaml\"\n\n  if [[ -f \"${dest}\" ]] \u0026\u0026 ! \"${FORCE}\"; then\n    skip \"${name} (already installed)\"\n    continue\n  fi\n\n  cp \"$f\" \"${dest}\"\n\n  if ! out=$(\"${DAEMON}\" sign \"${dest}\" --signer \"${FPR}\" 2\u003e\u00261); then\n    bad \"${name}: sign failed\"\n    printf '      %s\\n' \"${out}\"\n    rm -f \"${dest}\"   # never leave an unsigned file for LoadCommands to reject on every start\n    failed=$((failed + 1))\n    continue\n  fi\n\n  if ! out=$(\"${DAEMON}\" verify \"${dest}\" 2\u003e\u00261); then\n    bad \"${name}: signed but verification failed -- removing\"\n    printf '      %s\\n' \"${out}\"\n    rm -f \"${dest}\"\n    failed=$((failed + 1))\n    continue\n  fi\n\n  ok \"${name} signed and verified\"\n  done_n=$((done_n + 1))\ndone\n\nsec 'Summary'\nprintf '  %d installed, %d failed\\n' \"${done_n}\" \"${failed}\"\nif [[ \"${failed}\" -eq 0 \u0026\u0026 \"${done_n}\" -gt 0 ]]; then\n  printf '\\n  Start the daemon:  %s run\\n' \"${DAEMON}\"\n  printf '  It should log: commands loaded count=%d\\n\\n' \"$(find \"${COMMANDS_DIR}\" -maxdepth 1 -name '*.yaml' | wc -l)\"\nfi\n[[ \"${failed}\" -eq 0 ]]\n","file_path":"~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes/.bin/beadle-recipes-install.sh"},"tool_input_hash":"cacf272973c3bd7a94ffd0aa31f04265aed5948c63638c5110c906706ffb75d1","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# Sign beadle's example recipes and install them where the daemon loads them.\\n# Usage: beadle-recipes-install.sh --apply [--recipe NAME] [--repo DIR] [--force]\\nset -..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:09:03.898058671Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \"$W\"; chmod +x .bin/beadle-recipes-*.sh; for s in .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh .bin/beadle-recipes-install.sh; do printf \"%-38s \" \"$s\"; shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR \"$s\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\u0026 echo \"shellcheck clean\" || { echo \"ISSUES:\"; shellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR \"$s\" 2\u003e\u00261 | head -12; }; done; echo \"=== safety checker ===\"; for s in .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh .bin/beadle-recipes-install.sh; do printf \"%-38s \" \"$s\"; python3 .bin/health/script-safety.py \"$s\" \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e\u00261 \u0026\u0026 echo \"0 violations\" || echo \"flagged\"; done","description":"Shellcheck and safety-check both scripts"},"tool_input_hash":"592ad31393cca63d045a86b23d3100e9e08e28b7407f401ef3263ad327ee5936","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \\\"$W\\\"; chmod +x .bin/beadle-recipes-*.sh; for s in .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh .bin/beadle-recipes-install.sh; do printf \\\"%-38s..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:09:10.458241494Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \"$W\"; python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\np='.bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''  printf '  would run: %s init --fingerprint \u003cfpr\u003e%s\\\\n' \"${DAEMON}\" \"$(\"${FORCE}\" \u0026\u0026 echo ' --force' || true)\"'''\nnew='''  forceflag=''\n  \"${FORCE}\" \u0026\u0026 forceflag=' --force'\n  printf '  would run: %s init --fingerprint \u003cfpr\u003e%s\\\\n' \"${DAEMON}\" \"${forceflag}\"'''\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nPY\nshellcheck -x -P SCRIPTDIR .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh \u0026\u0026 echo \"init: shellcheck clean\"\necho \"=== preview: init (no --apply) ===\"; .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh --repo \u003crepo\u003e 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -22","description":"Fix SC2015 and preview the init script"},"tool_input_hash":"c617a42d7a62ea22176db0e2bd78f00325a7aa9a8d42e35d1ccac206c08412ba","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \\\"$W\\\"; python3 - \\u003c\\u003c'PY'\\np='.bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh'\\ns=open(p).read()\\nold='''  printf '  would run: %s init --fi..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:09:25.666412753Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \"$W\"; echo \"=== does 'false \u0026\u0026 x' kill the script under set -e? ===\"; bash -c 'set -euo pipefail; F=false; \"$F\" \u0026\u0026 v=1; echo \"SURVIVED\"' 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2; echo; echo \"=== preview with an expiring key (claude's) ===\"; .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh --fingerprint 2C7C808DEC5ECC59A23E4358C48E101AB522FB17 --repo \u003crepo\u003e 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -14","description":"Test the set -e hazard and run a full preview"},"tool_input_hash":"4a0d8530c3b4173d6d4edb988a0437ebd9cd3f6bd230bcf6670a26eb03dc4549","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \\\"$W\\\"; echo \\\"=== does 'false \\u0026\\u0026 x' kill the script under set -e? ===\\\"; bash -c 'set -euo pipefail; F=false; \\\"$F\\\" \\..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:09:34.22974511Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \"$W\"; B=\u003crepo\u003e\necho \"=== init with the non-expiring key (must refuse) ===\"; .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh --fingerprint 24A9B79FA94101C11F09A011CEE670F91FB96851 --repo \"$B\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -14; echo \"exit: ${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"\necho; echo \"=== install preview (no daemon.json yet) ===\"; .bin/beadle-recipes-install.sh --repo \"$B\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -6","description":"Test the expiry guard and install preview"},"tool_input_hash":"5c4ccbc71e810ee909701983327bf2e2a37c50659ff1299c2bbb074d766dc968","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \\\"$W\\\"; B=\\u003crepo\\u003e\\necho \\\"=== init with the non-expiring key (must refuse) ===\\\"; .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh --fingerpr..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:09:52.030373251Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \"$W\"; python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\np='.bin/README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor='## 2. Git operations'\nassert anchor in s\nrows = \"\"\"| `beadle-recipes-init.sh` | Configure `beadle-daemon`'s authorizer key: write `~/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json`, after checking the key is in the keyring and satisfies beadle's non-expiring-key invariant | `--apply [--fingerprint FPR] [--repo DIR] [--force]` | destructive (previews by default, `--apply` required: writes `daemon.json`. Reads the fingerprint from `pass beadle/authorizer-fingerprint`; never takes a secret on the command line, never modifies a GPG key — it prints the `gpg --quick-set-expire` command instead) |\n| `beadle-recipes-install.sh` | Sign `beadle`'s `examples/recipes/*.yaml` with the authorizer key named in `daemon.json` and install them where the daemon loads them | `--apply [--recipe NAME] [--repo DIR] [--force]` | destructive (previews by default, `--apply` required: writes `~/.punt-labs/beadle/commands/` and signs with the operator's real key. Removes any recipe that fails to sign or verify rather than leaving an unsigned file the daemon rejects on every start) |\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s.replace(anchor, rows + anchor, 1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnpx --yes markdownlint-cli2 .bin/README.md 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2; git add .bin/beadle-recipes-init.sh .bin/beadle-recipes-install.sh .bin/README.md \u0026\u0026 git commit -q -m \"chore(.bin): add beadle recipe init and install scripts\n\nTwo scripts covering the operator path that beadle-7gm's tooling makes\npossible but does not automate: name an authorizer key, then sign and\ninstall the example recipes where the daemon reads them.\n\nBoth preview by default and require --apply, per shell.md. Both resolve\nbeadle as a SCRIPT_DIR-relative sibling rather than a hardcoded home\npath. Neither accepts a secret as an argument.\n\nbeadle-recipes-init.sh reads the fingerprint from\n'pass beadle/authorizer-fingerprint' -- one place to look and one place\nto rotate, shared by humans and scripts. It deliberately does NOT modify\nthe operator's GPG key: beadle rejects non-expiring signing keys, and\nmost personal keys never expire, so it checks the primary AND signing\nsubkeys and prints the exact gpg --quick-set-expire commands instead of\nreaching into an identity key on its own initiative. Verified against a\nreal non-expiring key: it refuses with exit 1 and names the fix.\n\nbeadle-recipes-install.sh reads the authorizer from daemon.json rather\nthan a flag -- the daemon verifies against exactly that key, so taking\nit from anywhere else would install recipes the daemon then refuses. A\nrecipe that fails to sign or verify is removed rather than left in\nplace: LoadCommands correctly rejects an unsigned file, but logs an\nerror for it on every startup, so a half-installed recipe becomes\npermanent noise pointing at the wrong problem.\n\nshellcheck clean, script-safety.py 0 violations, both previews and both\nrefusal paths exercised.\" \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline -1","description":"Add README rows and commit"},"tool_input_hash":"60f2215cf2ebe3104887e3b6401e3be2175a76a8053acff03937af1734857c52","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"W=~/Coding/punt-labs/.claude/worktrees/install-recipes; cd \\\"$W\\\"; python3 - \\u003c\\u003c'PY'\\np='.bin/README.md'\\ns=open(p).read()\\nanchor='## 2. Git operations'\\nassert anchor in s\\nrows..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:14:25.494107112Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"echo \"=== key expiry now? ===\"; gpg --list-keys --with-colons 24A9B79FA94101C11F09A011CEE670F91FB96851 2\u003e/dev/null | awk -F: '$1==\"pub\"||$1==\"sub\"{printf \"  %-4s cap=%-6s expires=%s\\n\",$1,$12,($7==\"\"?\"NEVER\":strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\",$7))}'; echo \"=== pass entry? ===\"; pass show beadle/authorizer-fingerprint 2\u003e/dev/null | head -1 | sed 's/^\\(.\\{8\\}\\).*\\(.\\{8\\}\\)$/  \\1...\\2 (40-hex present)/' || echo \"  NOT readable\"","description":"Verify the gpg expiry and pass entry"},"tool_input_hash":"3e17db2e30c365b95fb5143051ac10e3224f18f02e6eaa42ea69d84a47df1b5d","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"echo \\\"=== key expiry now? ===\\\"; gpg --list-keys --with-colons 24A9B79FA94101C11F09A011CEE670F91FB96851 2\\u003e/dev/null | awk -F: '$1==\\\"pub\\\"||$1==\\\"sub\\\"{printf \\\"  %-4s cap=%-6s expir..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:17:30.459091443Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; echo \"=== installed recipes ===\"; ls -la ~/.punt-labs/beadle/commands/ | tail -4; echo \"=== each verifies against daemon.json's key? ===\"; for f in ~/.punt-labs/beadle/commands/*.yaml; do printf \"%-14s \" \"$(basename \"$f\" .yaml)\"; ./beadle-daemon verify \"$f\" 2\u003e\u00261 | sed 's/.*: //'; done; echo \"=== daemon.json ===\"; cat ~/.punt-labs/beadle/daemon.json","description":"Verify the installed recipes independently"},"tool_input_hash":"2f29d8c1359729f7349cf60f709c7d6bc9f42f98fb9612b790da6dc30e7238ec","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; echo \\\"=== installed recipes ===\\\"; ls -la ~/.punt-labs/beadle/commands/ | tail -4; echo \\\"=== each verifies against daemon.json's key? ===\\\"; for f in ~/.pu..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:27:39.977706051Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; echo \"=== poller interval + first-poll behaviour ===\"; grep -nE \"interval|Interval|first|ticker|Ticker\" internal/email/poller.go | head -14","description":"Find the poll interval logic"},"tool_input_hash":"e8928541b4c43d16fd59a69616054beff6938be511d97f96056130355b3e01e1","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; echo \\\"=== poller interval + first-poll behaviour ===\\\"; grep -nE \\\"interval|Interval|first|ticker|Ticker\\\" internal/email/poller.go | head -14\",\"description..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:27:45.347672308Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; echo \"=== your configured interval ===\"; grep -o '\"poll_interval\"[^,}]*' ~/.punt-labs/beadle/identities/[REDACTED:email]/email.json 2\u003e/dev/null || echo \"  poll_interval not set in identity config\"; echo \"=== what the daemon does when it is unset ===\"; grep -n -B3 -A8 \"Start reads the identity config\" internal/email/poller.go | head -20","description":"Check the configured interval and the unset behaviour"},"tool_input_hash":"2a3e32e5c8a99d96109bf50bf871d6dd700262e3abd72343c5626b65923fcb36","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; echo \\\"=== your configured interval ===\\\"; grep -o '\\\"poll_interval\\\"[^,}]*' ~/.punt-labs/beadle/identities/[REDACTED:email]/email.json 2\\u003e/dev/null ..."}
