{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:30:58.673470184Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"C=~/.punt-labs/beadle/identities/[REDACTED:email]/email.json; cp \"$C\" /tmp/email.json.bak; python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\nimport json,os\np=os.path.expanduser('~/.punt-labs/beadle/identities/[REDACTED:email]/email.json')\nd=json.load(open(p)); before=d.get('poll_interval')\nd['poll_interval']='1m'\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint(f\"poll_interval: {before} -\u003e 1m\")\nPY\ngrep -o '\"poll_interval\"[^,}]*' \"$C\"; echo \"(backup at /tmp/email.json.bak)\"; echo \"=== allowed values ===\"; grep -rn \"1m\\\":\" internal/email/*.go | head -2","description":"Set poll interval to 1m"},"tool_input_hash":"20537bcf2f1083bd4736f9ad07b80c5dabe71d6ec84cf40eb4bfd225be1e6173","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"C=~/.punt-labs/beadle/identities/[REDACTED:email]/email.json; cp \\\"$C\\\" /tmp/email.json.bak; python3 - \\u003c\\u003c'PY'\\nimport json,os\\np=os.path.expanduser('~/.punt-labs/beadle/ident..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:31:19.658552616Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; sed -n '180,195p' internal/email/config.go; bd create --title=\"poll intervals jump 1m to 5m with a 30m default — wrong shape for an agent mailbox\" --type=bug --priority=2 --description=\"OPERATOR FEEDBACK (2026-09-01): 'That's [REDACTED:profanity]. It needs to run every 3m at the max.'\n\nTwo problems, one config and one code.\n\n1. THE DEFAULT IS 30m. ~/.punt-labs/beadle/identities/[REDACTED:email]/email.json shipped with poll_interval: 30m. For a mailbox whose entire purpose is letting someone direct an agent by email, a half-hour worst-case latency makes the channel feel broken. Someone sends mail, nothing happens, they assume it failed. Set to 1m by hand to run the demo.\n\n2. THE ALLOWED SET HAS NO USABLE MIDDLE. validPollIntervals (internal/email/config.go:180-190) is 1m, 5m, 10m, 15m, 30m, 1h, 2h. The operator asked for 3m as a ceiling and there is nothing between 1m and 5m to pick. So the only value satisfying 'no slower than 3m' is 1m, which is more aggressive than anyone actually wants as a steady state.\n\nWHAT TO CHANGE:\n  - Add 2m and 3m to validPollIntervals.\n  - Reconsider the default. 30m is defensible for a human's archive mailbox and wrong for an agent's inbox; 3m or 5m is the sane default here.\n  - The MCP set_poll_interval tool and the /inbox skill's interval table both enumerate the same set and must stay in sync -- plugin/commands/inbox.md lists 1m/5m/10m/15m/30m/1h/2h with matching cron expressions.\n\nWORTH NOTING while changing this: Poller suppresses new-mail callbacks on its first poll after startup, by design, so a restart does not reprocess the backlog. Combined with a 30m interval that means the first message after a restart could wait an hour. The suppression is correct; the interval is what makes it painful.\n\nAlso why the daemon test tier drives OnNewMail directly rather than through Poller (docs/TESTING.md): the 1m floor and first-poll suppression make Poller unusable in a pre-commit gate. Lowering the floor does not change that, but adding 2m/3m does not help testing either -- do not conflate the two.\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2","description":"File the poll interval design bead"},"tool_input_hash":"879b7643a89eba553f8750b1997323a34d820d6d5e71d43d01af131a58ee13b9","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; sed -n '180,195p' internal/email/config.go; bd create --title=\\\"poll intervals jump 1m to 5m with a 30m default — wrong shape for an agent mailbox\\\" --type..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T12:34:50.294746202Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; grep -n -B4 -A14 \"first\" internal/email/poller.go | grep -A14 -B4 \"notify\\|unseen\" | head -24","description":"Confirm first-poll suppression behaviour"},"tool_input_hash":"b8d90715c368b53786554b6ddac7d9c3e982475cf8d7db2c2a38beffdfde194e","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; grep -n -B4 -A14 \\\"first\\\" internal/email/poller.go | grep -A14 -B4 \\\"notify\\\\|unseen\\\" | head -24\",\"description\":\"Confirm first-poll suppression behaviour\"}"}
