{"ts":"2026-09-01T13:46:04.6967475Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; git log --oneline -1; git status --short | grep -v \"^??\\|kwb.md\\|vox.md\"; echo \"--- branch ---\"; git branch --show-current; echo \"=== spawner Run signature ===\"; grep -n \"func (s \\*WorkerSpawner) Run\\|func.*Spawner interface\" -A6 internal/daemon/spawner.go | head -14","description":"Check branch state and the Spawner interface"},"tool_input_hash":"edf50e9cde011a7ece12a6538d2c4e2507dd533f4e4277a81c3d0a81e4f468c7","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; git log --oneline -1; git status --short | grep -v \\\"^??\\\\|kwb.md\\\\|vox.md\\\"; echo \\\"--- branch ---\\\"; git branch --show-current; echo \\\"=== spawner Run sign..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T13:46:22.58714136Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; cat \u003e .tmp/missions/tools-and-body.yaml \u003c\u003c'YAML'\nleader: claude\nworker: bwk\nevaluator:\n  handle: djb\ninputs:\n  ticket: beadle-ivtd\nwrite_set:\n  - internal/daemon/spawner.go\n  - internal/daemon/spawner_test.go\n  - internal/daemon/runner.go\n  - internal/daemon/runner_test.go\n  - internal/daemon/pipeline.go\n  - internal/daemon/pipeline_test.go\n  - internal/daemon/pipeline_edge_test.go\n  - internal/daemon/mission.go\n  - internal/daemon/mission_test.go\n  - internal/daemon/command.go\n  - internal/daemon/command_test.go\n  - internal/daemon/handler.go\n  - internal/daemon/harness_test.go\n  - internal/daemontest/daemontest.go\n  - cmd/beadle-daemon/main.go\n  - examples/recipes/summarize.yaml\n  - examples/recipes/sysreport.yaml\n  - examples/recipes/docs-ask.yaml\n  - examples/recipes/reply.yaml\n  - examples/recipes/README.md\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - \"FIX 1 -- tools come from the recipe. Command.Tools exists, is parsed, and is referenced NOWHERE (grep -rn '\\\\.Tools' returns nothing outside tests). spawner.go:94 hardcodes --allowedTools Bash,Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep,Agent for every worker. Thread cmd.Tools through to the spawner and pass only what the recipe declares.\"\n  - \"FIX 1 -- a recipe declaring no tools gets NO tools. Empty must mean none, not a default set. summarize needs zero and currently gets a shell.\"\n  - \"FIX 1 -- validateCommand rejects unknown tool names against a known set, so a typo fails at load rather than silently granting nothing (or everything).\"\n  - \"FIX 2 -- pass the email body instead of making the worker fetch it. Executor.Run already receives body; stageContext and the mission contract must carry it. Remove the success_criteria line telling the worker to read the mailbox via beadle-email using inputs.trigger.\"\n  - \"FIX 2 -- delete the fake arg. main.go's rule passes {\\\"text\\\": \\\"see email body\\\"}, a literal placeholder that is not the body. Either pass the real body or pass nothing; do not carry the lie forward.\"\n  - \"FIX 2 -- the body is adversarial input. Cap it (maxContractFieldRunes exists) and keep escapeYAMLValue's treatment; it must not break contract YAML or reach a log.\"\n  - \"Update all four example recipes to declare the tools they actually need. summarize: none. reply: none beyond its MCP server. sysreport and docs-ask: whatever they genuinely use.\"\n  - \"Tests: a worker spawned for a recipe with no tools gets no --allowedTools grant; a recipe declaring Read gets Read and not Bash; the body reaches the contract; an unknown tool name fails validation.\"\n  - \"make check passes. Commit per fix, each green. Do not push.\"\nbudget:\n  rounds: 2\n  reflection_after_each: true\nYAML\nethos mission create --file .tmp/missions/tools-and-body.yaml 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -2","description":"Create the mission for both fixes"},"tool_input_hash":"c82e029acf521c9f170c7b048716f46d431ccb114e12dbd95b2351699b5584c8","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; cat \\u003e .tmp/missions/tools-and-body.yaml \\u003c\\u003c'YAML'\\nleader: claude\\nworker: bwk\\nevaluator:\\n  handle: djb\\ninputs:\\n  ticket: beadle-ivtd\\nwrit..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T13:46:41.304329261Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-09-01-013","contract_id":"m-2026-09-01-005","tool":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Wire recipe tools and pass the email body","name":"tools-and-body","prompt":"Mission `m-2026-09-01-005`. Read it: `ethos mission show m-2026-09-01-005`. Branch `feat/summarize-recipe` in \u003crepo\u003e, checked out. Two fixes, both found by the operator during the first real end-to-end daemon run.\n\n**FIX 1 — a recipe's declared tools are ignored.**\n\n`Command.Tools []string` is in the schema, parsed from YAML, and referenced **nowhere**: `grep -rn '\\.Tools' internal/ cmd/ --include='*.go'` (excluding tests) returns nothing. Meanwhile `spawner.go:94` hardcodes `--allowedTools Bash,Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep,Agent` for every worker.\n\nConsequence, observed live: `summarize.yaml` declares `mcp_servers: []` and needs no filesystem access. It was handed a shell, used it to run `beadle-email` and read the operator's inbox, and produced a correct summary that way. It worked by accident of an undeclared capability.\n\nNote the asymmetry to fix toward: `mcp_servers` **is** honoured — `BuildMCPConfig` gives a worker only the servers its recipe names. Tools should work the same way. Half the capability surface is recipe-scoped and signed; the other half is a constant.\n\nThread `cmd.Tools` to the spawner. **Empty means none, not a default set.** A recipe that declares nothing gets nothing. Add validation against a known tool set so a typo fails at load rather than silently granting nothing.\n\n**FIX 2 — the email body is not passed; the worker is told to go get it.**\n\n`mission.go`'s contract carries only `message_id`, `from`, `subject`, plus this success criterion: *\"Read the email via beadle-email tools using the message ID in inputs.trigger.\"* And `main.go`'s rule passes `{\"text\": \"see email body\"}` — a literal placeholder string, not content. `stageContext` renders it as `stage args: text=see email body`.\n\n`Executor.Run(ctx, meta, body)` already **has** the body. Pass it. Then drop the read-the-mailbox instruction and delete the fake arg.\n\nThe operator's reasoning, which I agree with: making the worker fetch its own input requires granting mailbox access for a single-message task — it can then read *any* message. Passing the content grants nothing. The body reaches the model either way, so the capability is the only real difference, and least privilege wins. The cost is the body landing in the contract and the on-disk pipeline record, which is bounded and already pruned.\n\nTreat the body as adversarial input: cap it (`maxContractFieldRunes` exists), keep `escapeYAMLValue`'s handling so it cannot break contract YAML, and keep it out of logs.\n\n**These two fixes are related and land together.** Fix 2 is what makes Fix 1 safe — remove the shell without passing the body and `summarize` stops working, because its only route to the content today is that shell.\n\nAlso update all four example recipes to declare what they actually need. `summarize`: none. `reply`: nothing beyond its MCP server. `sysreport` and `docs-ask`: whatever they genuinely use.\n\n`make check` before each commit, one commit per fix. Do not push. Submit with `ethos mission result m-2026-09-01-005 --file \u003cpath\u003e`. If the write-set is short, escalate — do not reach outside it.","subagent_type":"bwk"},"tool_input_hash":"699b86e043684bc314258c864827e9bdbba38ebe5008825a6913035eafa62d91","tool_input_preview":"{\"description\":\"Wire recipe tools and pass the email body\",\"name\":\"tools-and-body\",\"prompt\":\"Mission `m-2026-09-01-005`. Read it: `ethos mission show m-2026-09-01-005`. Branch `feat/summarize-recipe` ..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T13:55:27.574592862Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-09-01-013","contract_id":"m-2026-09-01-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"B=\u003crepo\u003e; cd \"$B\"; echo \"=== working tree changes ===\"; git status --short | grep -v \"^??\\|kwb.md\\|vox.md\"; echo \"=== most recent mtime in the write-set ===\"; find internal/daemon cmd/beadle-daemon examples/recipes -newermt '-15 minutes' -type f 2\u003e/dev/null | head -5; echo \"=== now: $(date '+%H:%M:%S') ===\"; git log --oneline -1","description":"Check for filesystem activity"},"tool_input_hash":"e6b3e0933cd460236bba2f91bfc802b815f2781f03e52cd4d0d10e1ea468e246","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"B=\\u003crepo\\u003e; cd \\\"$B\\\"; echo \\\"=== working tree changes ===\\\"; git status --short | grep -v \\\"^??\\\\|kwb.md\\\\|vox.md\\\"; echo \\\"=== most recent mtime in the write-set ===\\\"; find inte..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T13:55:43.989751661Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-09-01-013","contract_id":"m-2026-09-01-005","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Status check. No file changes in the write-set an…","message":"Status check. No file changes in the write-set and a clean working tree — you have been reading for a while. That is fine if you are still mapping the call path; I judge progress by the filesystem, not by commits, and analysis is invisible.\n\nReply with one line: what you are working out, and whether you are blocked.\n\nIf something in the brief is wrong or underspecified, say so — I would rather rescope than have you work around it. Two things I can imagine tripping you up:\n\n**How `--allowedTools` interacts with MCP tools.** I measured this earlier: a worker spawned with `--allowedTools \"Bash,Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep,Agent\"` — no MCP tool named — still successfully called `mcp__context7__resolve-library-id`. `--permission-mode auto` appears to cover MCP tools regardless of the allowlist. So \"empty tools means no tools\" may not hold for MCP tools the way it does for built-ins. If that is what you are chasing: it is a real complication, tell me and we will decide rather than you guessing.\n\n**Whether removing the shell breaks `summarize` before Fix 2 lands.** It does — that is why the two ship together. If you are sequencing commits and hit a state where `make check` fails between them, that is expected; combine them into one commit rather than leaving a broken intermediate.\n\nNot asking you to hurry. Asking you to tell me where you are.","recipient":"tools-and-body","summary":"Status check — no edits yet","to":"tools-and-body","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"5e9ca02f5a57e6df85c2eb25dcfaf8b57d0b372fe64f1252f944cb23077bb4e9","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"Status check. No file changes in the write-set an…\",\"message\":\"Status check. No file changes in the write-set and a clean working tree — you have been reading for a while. That is fine..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T13:57:52.670960363Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-09-01-013","contract_id":"m-2026-09-01-005","tool":"Write","tool_input":{"content":"---\nname: feedback_resume-agents-never-restart\ndescription: \"Resume a running agent with SendMessage; never TaskStop one that has paid a large context-loading cost\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nAn agent that has spent minutes reading a codebase holds that understanding in its context. Resume\nit with `SendMessage` to its name or ID — the context survives. A fresh `Agent()` call starts from\nzero and re-pays the entire read.\n\n**Why:** loading cost is real and invisible. A worker on a capability-boundary or trust-model change\nmay legitimately read for ten minutes before touching a file, and the filesystem shows nothing the\nwhole time. Killing it there discards the expensive part and buys nothing — the replacement does the\nsame reading again, slower, because it also has to re-derive whatever the first one had already\nworked out. The operator's framing: \"if it takes 10m to read the code to start, that's a cost we do\nnot want to pay over and over.\"\n\n**How to apply:** silence is not a stall. Judge progress by whether the working tree is changing over\na long window, and when unsure send a status ping rather than acting — ask what it is working out and\nwhether it is blocked, and name the specific complication you suspect so it can confirm or correct\nyou cheaply. Reserve `TaskStop` for an agent that is genuinely unresponsive *and* not editing, and\nprefer suspending over stopping in every other case. See [[feedback_write-set-cannot-be-amended]] for\nthe related point that a worker flagging a scope problem is doing its job, not stalling.\n","file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-beadle/memory/feedback_resume-agents-never-restart.md"},"tool_input_hash":"7d6367a81402aa92c26bb05f1390e0691fb9abcf62a5fe56d59aefa1d1fd4b63","tool_input_preview":"{\"content\":\"---\\nname: feedback_resume-agents-never-restart\\ndescription: \\\"Resume a running agent with SendMessage; never TaskStop one that has paid a large context-loading cost\\\"\\nmetadata:\\n  type:..."}
{"ts":"2026-09-01T13:57:57.990092846Z","session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","parent_session":"db7ba632-660e-41c7-bace-799ed3f6d8a2","delegation_id":"d-2026-09-01-013","contract_id":"m-2026-09-01-005","tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"M=~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-beadle/memory; grep -q \"resume-agents-never-restart\" \"$M/MEMORY.md\" || printf -- '- [Resume agents, never restart](feedback_resume-agents-never-restart.md) — SendMessage keeps context; a fresh Agent() re-pays the whole read.\\n' \u003e\u003e \"$M/MEMORY.md\"; tail -2 \"$M/MEMORY.md\"","description":"Index the memory"},"tool_input_hash":"12e79123c3a6ce2cc932d2946a2a63c90260fe92919a4594933e49056c700666","tool_input_preview":"{\"command\":\"M=~/.claude/projects/-home-jfreeman-Coding-punt-labs-beadle/memory; grep -q \\\"resume-agents-never-restart\\\" \\\"$M/MEMORY.md\\\" || printf -- '- [Resume agents, never restart](feedback_resume-..."}
